        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3412620/extras/a674ef62cd48ebdbfa1c2357c5502a9c.avif?t=1779824897\" width=616 height=100 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ethel Briggs is a shy, self-conscious girl in her final year of university. Though she should be working on her thesis about Romantic poetry, her well of inspiration has run dry. After a nasty break-up with her former girlfriend, Clementine, Ethel is feeling very blue — and it certainly doesn't help that she's spending the winter holidays in the depressingly drab village of Oxbury, while her family are off holidaying in sunny Australia. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <br>Left to her own devices, Ethel struggles to finish her thesis while the cold, wintry wind blows outside and the days continue to get shorter and darker. <br><br>Staying inside proves to be unbearable, however, and Ethel escapes the confines of her family's home for a breath of fresh air. Going for a walk in the woods should be enough to invigorate her, and fill her with newfound passion for Romanticism. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >That was Ethel's plan, at least — but she wasn't counting on meeting a mysterious, dark-haired beauty in the woods, who is much more than she seems.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3412620/extras/eaad616869232f3e5318bde8b5d67248.avif?t=1779824897\" width=616 height=100 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- 50,000 words of text (approx 2-4 hours of reading) <br>- A linear story with only one ending  <br>- Original character and background art  <br>- An original soundtrack  <br>- A dark lesbian rom